import LeanModels.Sv.Ingest2
import LeanModels.Sv.CombSigned

/-!
# `comb_signed`: signed declarations and signed reads in the `sv_comb` fragment

The loader reads a signed signal as the cast marker around the identifier (`PExpr.cast true (.ident n)`), and keeps the
signedness of each declaration (`Decl.isSigned`). The tactics summarize the UNSIGNED TWIN of such a design
(`PDesign.unsign`: every signed read in an operand of a continuous assign replaced by the unsigned read of the same
signal) and carry each theorem back to the design as written along `instantiateGD2_unsign_view` (`CombSigned.lean`),
under the width obligation of `sv_equations` (no operand is implicitly widened, so no signed operand is ever extended).

* `sadd.sv`: two's-complement `+` and `-` on signed operands of one width, a bitwise mix, and a signed input copied to an
  unsigned output (`comb_proof.lean` proves all four for every width);
* `pass.sv`: a signed input copied to an unsigned output of the same width;
* `scmp.sv`: the four signed comparisons `<`, `<=`, `>`, `>=` of two signed inputs of one width. The unsigned twin keeps
  them as written (`PExpr.unsign` does not enter an operator whose meaning signedness changes), the recognizer reads each
  as a signed comparison of two signed signals declared with the same dimensions, and `sv_equations` states its bit
  through `BitVec.slt`/`BitVec.sle` (`comb_proof.lean` proves all four for every width);
* `scmp_const.sv`: signed comparisons of a signed signal with a constant, the constant on either side: an 8-bit signed
  signal against sized signed literals of its width (`8'sd0`, `8'sd100`, and `-3` written as its bits `8'sb1111_1101`),
  a 32-bit signed signal against unsized constants (`0`, `5`, 32-bit signed integers). No operand is extended (the
  literal is as wide as the signal; the signal is as wide as the unsized constant), so the recognizer reads them when
  the signal is declared with constant dimensions of that width (`scmpRd?`); `comb_proof.lean`, `scmp_const_correct`,
  states each bit as the order of the two's-complement integers (`u.toInt < -3`, ...);
* `asr.sv`: the arithmetic shift right `>>>` of a signed input by an unsigned amount (a signal and the constant `1`), and
  the left shift `<<` of a signed input, into targets of the operand's width (`comb_proof.lean`: `BitVec.sshiftRight` and
  `<<<` for every width);
* `asr_proc.sv`: the same `>>>` inside `always_comb`, which the procedural route reads too;
* `signed_decl.sv` (the clean-room repro, verbatim below its header), `scmp_mixed.sv`, `scmp_sext.sv`, `scmp_sext_w.sv`:
  signed comparisons whose narrower operand is sign-extended to the comparison's width (IEEE 1800-2023 §11.8.2, §11.6.1),
  which the envelope marks `SignedResize` (the loader reads a signed literal under a marker of its own): `x >= 0` with an
  8-bit `x` (extended to the 32 bits of the unsized constant), `x < w` of an 8-bit and a 16-bit signal, a signal against
  signed literals of its width, wider and narrower, and `x >= 0` with `x` of a parameter width `W` (extended where
  `W < 32`; at `W ≥ 32` the constant is materialized at `W`). The skeleton reads the marker as `Sk.sx` (sign extension to
  the context, `Expr2.resizeSigned`, at every width) and the recognizer reads it against an unsized constant, another
  marked operand, or a signal declared with constant dimensions at least as wide (`scmpSxRd?`); `comb_proof.lean` proves
  each bit as the order of the two's-complement integers;
* `ssel.sv`: bit and part selects of signed inputs, unsigned values (IEEE 1800-2023 §11.8.1): the sign bit, the low bits,
  a bit inside `^`, and `{a[W-1], a[W-1:1]}` (`comb_proof.lean`, for every width `W ≥ 2`). The twin reads each select
  of the plain signal;
* `neg/`: the constructs whose meaning signedness changes and the tactics do not read yet, refused with that reason
  (`comb_errors.lean`): a select of a signed signal inside `always_comb`, a signed comparison of
  two signals declared with different dimensions, one in a self-determined position, one of an operand that is not a whole signal, and one inside
  `always_comb`; an arithmetic shift right by a signed amount and in a self-determined position, and `>>>` of an unsigned
  operand. (A select of a signed signal as a shift operand, and `>>>` into a wider target, are read since the left
  operand of a shift is read through `instDivOperand2`: `comb_shift`, `shift_signed_correct`.) (Sign extension into a wider target, `neg/sg_ext.sv`, never reaches the tactics: at a
  symbolic width the extractor marks the conversion `ConversionExpression:width`; so does a signed comparison of two
  operands whose widths differ symbolically.)

The envelopes were generated by
`python3.12 extractors/sv/extract.py --top <module> Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/<file>.sv -o <file>.sv.json`.
-/

namespace Examples.«system-verilog».comb_signed.gen

open LeanModels.Sv LeanModels.Sv.CombView

load_design_sv2 sadd from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/sadd.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 pass from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/pass.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 scmp from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/scmp.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 scmp_const from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/scmp_const.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 asr from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/asr.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 asr_proc from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/asr_proc.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 ssel from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/ssel.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 signed_decl from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/signed_decl.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 scmp_mixed from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/scmp_mixed.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 scmp_sext from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/scmp_sext.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 scmp_sext_w from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_signed/scmp_sext_w.sv.json"

-- The design as written has signed reads: the recognizer refuses them, and summarizes the unsigned twin.
#guard sadd.pdesign.summary.toOption.isNone
#guard sadd.pdesign.unsign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard (sadd.pdesign.unsign == sadd.pdesign) == false
#guard pass.pdesign.summary.toOption.isNone
#guard pass.pdesign.unsign.summary.toOption.isSome
-- A signed comparison is read as written: the twin is the design itself, and the recognizer accepts it.
#guard scmp.pdesign.unsign == scmp.pdesign
#guard scmp.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard scmp_const.pdesign.unsign == scmp_const.pdesign
#guard scmp_const.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
-- So is a shift of a signed operand (the twin does not enter a shift).
#guard asr.pdesign.unsign == asr.pdesign
#guard asr.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
-- A select of a signed signal is read through the twin (the select of the plain signal).
#guard ssel.pdesign.summary.toOption.isNone
#guard ssel.pdesign.unsign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard (ssel.pdesign.unsign == ssel.pdesign) == false

-- The declarations keep their signedness (the summary's too).
#guard (sadd.sem 8).decls.toList.map (·.isSigned) == [true, true, true, true, false, false]
#guard (sadd.pdesign.unsign.summary.toOption.map fun s => s.decls.map (·.isSigned)) ==
  some [true, true, true, true, false, false]

-- A run at `W = 4`: `a = -3` (1101), `b = 5` (0101): `s = 2` (0010), `d = -8` (1000), `x = 1101 ^ ~0101 = 0111`,
-- `y = 1101`.
#guard (match run2 (sadd.sem 4) σ_src 1000 [[("a", .ofNat 4 13), ("b", .ofNat 4 5)]] with
  | .ok [st] =>
      (SvState.lookup st "s").map LVec.toBinString == some "0010" &&
      (SvState.lookup st "d").map LVec.toBinString == some "1000" &&
      (SvState.lookup st "x").map LVec.toBinString == some "0111" &&
      (SvState.lookup st "y").map LVec.toBinString == some "1101"
  | _ => false)

-- A run at `W = 4`, `a = -3` (1101), `b = 5` (0101): signed, `a < b` (unsigned, 13 > 5): `lt = le = 1`, `gt = ge = 0`;
-- and at `a = b = -3`: `le = ge = 1`, `lt = gt = 0`.
#guard (match run2 (scmp.sem 4) σ_src 1000
    [[("a", .ofNat 4 13), ("b", .ofNat 4 5)], [("a", .ofNat 4 13), ("b", .ofNat 4 13)]] with
  | .ok [s1, s2] =>
      [("lt", "1"), ("le", "1"), ("gt", "0"), ("ge", "0")].all (fun (n, v) =>
        (SvState.lookup s1 n).map LVec.toBinString == some v) &&
      [("lt", "0"), ("le", "1"), ("gt", "0"), ("ge", "1")].all (fun (n, v) =>
        (SvState.lookup s2 n).map LVec.toBinString == some v)
  | _ => false)

-- Runs of `scmp_const.sv`, the bits in the order `x_ge0 x_le0r x_ltm3 x_gt100r z_ge0 z_lt5 z_le0r`, each the value
-- Icarus Verilog 12.0 prints for the same inputs (`iverilog -g2012`): `x = -3`, `z = -1`: `0001010`; `x = -4`, `z = 5`:
-- `0011101`; `x = 100`, `z = 4`: `1100111`; `x = 99`, `z = -2^31`: `1101010`.
#guard [((253, 4294967295), "0001010"), ((252, 5), "0011101"), ((100, 4), "1100111"), ((99, 2147483648), "1101010")].all
  fun ((x, z), want) =>
    match run2 scmp_const.sem σ_src 1000 [[("x", .ofNat 8 x), ("z", .ofNat 32 z)]] with
    | .ok [st] =>
        (["x_ge0", "x_le0r", "x_ltm3", "x_gt100r", "z_ge0", "z_lt5", "z_le0r"].foldlM
          (fun acc n => (SvState.lookup st n).map fun v => acc ++ v.toBinString) "") == some want
    | _ => false

-- Sign-extended comparisons: the summary reads them as written (no signed read is left for the twin).
#guard signed_decl.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard scmp_mixed.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard scmp_sext.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard scmp_sext_w.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
-- The envelope's operand of `x >= 0` is the marker around the signed read; a signed literal is read under the loader's
-- marker too (`x >= 8'sd0`).
#guard (signed_decl.pdesign.processes.map fun p => match p with
  | .assign _ (.binary _ l r) => some (l, r)
  | _ => none) == [some (.signedResize 32 (.cast true (.ident "x")), .int 0)]
-- Runs of `scmp_sext.sv`, the bits in the order `x_ge0 x_lt5 w_ltm3 x_gt0r x_le_w`, and of `signed_decl.sv` and
-- `scmp_mixed.sv`, each the value local Icarus Verilog 12.0 prints for the same inputs: `x = -3`, `w = -4`: `01100`,
-- `0`, `0`; `x = 5`, `w = 5`: `10011`, `1`, `0`; `x = -128`, `w = -3`: `01001`, `0`, `1`.
#guard [((253, 65532), "01100", "0", "0"), ((5, 5), "10011", "1", "0"), ((128, 65533), "01001", "0", "1")].all
  fun ((x, w), want, wd, wm) =>
    (match run2 scmp_sext.sem σ_src 1000 [[("x", .ofNat 8 x), ("w", .ofNat 16 w)]] with
    | .ok [st] =>
        (["x_ge0", "x_lt5", "w_ltm3", "x_gt0r", "x_le_w"].foldlM
          (fun acc n => (SvState.lookup st n).map fun v => acc ++ v.toBinString) "") == some want
    | _ => false) &&
    (match run2 signed_decl.sem σ_src 1000 [[("x", .ofNat 8 x)]] with
    | .ok [st] => (SvState.lookup st "y").map LVec.toBinString == some wd
    | _ => false) &&
    (match run2 scmp_mixed.sem σ_src 1000 [[("x", .ofNat 8 x), ("w", .ofNat 16 w)]] with
    | .ok [st] => (SvState.lookup st "y").map LVec.toBinString == some wm
    | _ => false)
-- `scmp_sext_w.sv` at `W = 40` (`x` wider than the constant, compared at 40 bits: `0x0080000000` is positive although
-- its low 32 bits are not) and at `W = 4` (as Icarus 12.0: `0`, `1` at `W = 40`; `1`, `0` at `W = 4`).
#guard (match run2 (scmp_sext_w.sem 40) σ_src 1000 [[("x", .ofNat 40 0x8000000000)], [("x", .ofNat 40 0x0080000000)]] with
  | .ok [s1, s2] => (SvState.lookup s1 "y").map LVec.toBinString == some "0" &&
      (SvState.lookup s2 "y").map LVec.toBinString == some "1"
  | _ => false)
#guard (match run2 (scmp_sext_w.sem 4) σ_src 1000 [[("x", .ofNat 4 7)], [("x", .ofNat 4 8)]] with
  | .ok [s1, s2] => (SvState.lookup s1 "y").map LVec.toBinString == some "1" &&
      (SvState.lookup s2 "y").map LVec.toBinString == some "0"
  | _ => false)

-- A run at `W = 4`, `a = -6` (1010), `s = 1`: `y = a >>> 1 = -3` (1101), `z = 1101`, `l = a << 1 = 0100`; and at `s = 5`
-- (an amount of the width or more): `y = 1111` (all sign bits), `l = 0000`.
#guard (match run2 (asr.sem 4) σ_src 1000
    [[("a", .ofNat 4 10), ("s", .ofNat 3 1)], [("a", .ofNat 4 10), ("s", .ofNat 3 5)]] with
  | .ok [s1, s2] =>
      [("y", "1101"), ("z", "1101"), ("l", "0100")].all (fun (n, v) =>
        (SvState.lookup s1 n).map LVec.toBinString == some v) &&
      [("y", "1111"), ("z", "1101"), ("l", "0000")].all (fun (n, v) =>
        (SvState.lookup s2 n).map LVec.toBinString == some v)
  | _ => false)

-- A run at `W = 4`, `a = -6` (1010), `b = 5` (0101): `msb = 1`, `low = 010`, `x = a[0] ^ b[3] = 0`, `h = 1101`.
#guard (match run2 (ssel.sem 4) σ_src 1000 [[("a", .ofNat 4 10), ("b", .ofNat 4 5)]] with
  | .ok [st] =>
      [("msb", "1"), ("low", "010"), ("x", "0"), ("h", "1101")].all (fun (n, v) =>
        (SvState.lookup st n).map LVec.toBinString == some v)
  | _ => false)

end Examples.«system-verilog».comb_signed.gen
